    "caption": "While we wait for borders to open in Japan again, make this Yakiniku Donburi at home and be instantly transported to the Land of the Rising Sun through this simple yet tasty beef dish.\n\nWhen it comes to Japanese food, quality is everything, which is why we opted for Margaret River Wagyu Beef Yakiniku for this recipe. It’s a splurge well-worth it. Because the beef is highly marbled, expect rich and buttery flavors that cut through the marinade so effortlessly and perfectly.\n\nHungry yet? Head over to #TheMarketplace and find all the ingredients you need — including Margaret River Wagyu Beef products and other premium and imported beef brands. Our selection is unbeatable.\n\nServing Time: 45 minutes to 1 hour\nYield: 2 servings\n\nIngredients\n\n2 tbsps. soy sauce\n1 tbsp. mirin\n2 tbsps. sugar\n1 tbsps. garlic, grated\n1 tsp. ginger, grated\n2 tbsps. sesame seeds\n500g Margaret River Wagyu Beef Yakiniku\n1 tbsp. sesame oil\n2 tbsps. canola oil\n3 cups Japanese rice, cooked\n2 egg yolks\n½ cup scallions, curled\n\nProcedure\n\n1. In a large bowl, combine soy sauce, mirin, sugar, garlic, ginger, and a tablespoon of sesame seeds. Mix in Margaret River Wagyu Beef Yakiniku, and marinate for at least 30 minutes.\n2. Set a pan over medium heat, then add sesame oil and canola oil. Sear marinated Margaret River Wagyu Beef Yakiniku until nicely browned on both sides.\n3. Add Japanese rice in a bowl, then top with cooked Wagyu Beef and egg yolk on the middle. Garnish with scallions and the remaining sesame seeds. \n\nDid you know? You can now stay at home and order your groceries online at http://bit.ly/TheMarketplaceGoCart. Join our Viber community as well at https://bit.ly/TheMarketplaceViber!",
